cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ISLA in research, teaching, or another software project,
  please cite the released version you used. This file currently cites
  the latest published release, v4.0.0.
type: software
title: "ISLA — Let the Music Flow."
abstract: >-
  ISLA is an open-source audio-processing application for local file
  playback and experimental macOS system-audio monitoring. It provides
  Original/Bypass alongside Velvet, Legato, and Melt musical processing
  profiles through a Python terminal interface and a desktop Audio
  Control Center.
authors:
  - family-names: Feeney
    given-names: Don Michael
    name-suffix: Jr.
keywords:
  - audio signal processing
  - music
  - phase alignment
  - real-time audio
  - research software
  - Python
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dfeen87/ISLA"
